MICHELLE XU: And so
a little fun fact,

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:10.330
as you're watching
this play live.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:13.120
So there is a star
called a Betelgeuse.

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:17.780
It's only 600
light-years away from us.

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:21.500
And Betelgeuse is so big
that when they experience

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:24.870
a supernova, which scientists
do believe it is going to go--

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:28.510
it's going to explode soonish--

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:33.480
and if, and when that
happens in our lifetime,

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:36.840
when everybody else is
looking at this a bright blob

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:42.380
in the sky, and all of us,
here, where we can say,

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:44.390
meh, been there, done that.

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:50.653
We've seen that at Google
Cloud Next in 2019.

