00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:17.329
Here's our second demo from
a couple of our partners,

00:17:17.329 --> 00:17:19.160
actually.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:22.010
Do we all know what
preemptible VMs are?

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.240
Can I see a show of hands?

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:24.109
Preemptible VMs?

00:17:24.109 --> 00:17:24.800
Nice.

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:26.690
Good, nice.

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:31.670
For those who don't know what
preemptible VM is, the name

00:17:31.670 --> 00:17:35.360
itself is quite
self-explanatory.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.530
There is a trade-off, right?

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:39.180
You can spawn a VM and there's--
with a preemptible VMs,

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.200
there a trade-off.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:46.550
You can take risk of
jobs being preempted,

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:49.970
and at the same time, you
can enjoy the cost saving

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:53.208
of these preemptible VMs.

00:17:53.208 --> 00:17:55.750
And I can see you some people
are already shaking their heads

00:17:55.750 --> 00:18:00.180
because engineers do not
want to launch thousands

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.850
of batch jobs and wake
up in the morning knowing

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:03.870
that jobs are not done.

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:08.990
When we set up the--

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:14.510
our entire infrastructure with
a good scheduler and a good file

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:20.100
system in the back end, even
when the VMs are preempted,

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:24.960
the job scheduler can
recognize the preem--

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:27.570
the jobs are being
preempted, and save

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:30.870
the current state of the
job in the file system

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:32.160
in the back end.

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:34.050
And then put the job
back in the queue

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:38.850
and respawn it somewhere else,
and remount the file system.

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:43.410
And let's welcome David
from Elastifile and Brian

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:48.240
from SchedMD to show us
how to seamlessly manage

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:51.862
your preempted jobs
on Google Cloud.

